      "description": "* Automated Postal Center (APC): \n      - Developed the 508 compliance functionality for the United State Postal Services (USPS) kiosk.  The 508 compliance functionality ensures that the visually impaired have access to use the kiosk to mail a letter or package, buy stamps and look up information services. \nVia Voice and C++ were used to develop the 508 compliance functionality.\n     - Assisted in estimating task duration. \n     - Supported system testing and production implementation.\n     - Assisted in process definition and improvement.\n\n* High Performance Storage System (HPSS):\n     - Developed the graphical user and command line interface applications for HPSS system administrator to configure and manage HPSS system. HPSS is software that manages petabytes of data on disk and robotic tape libraries.\n       The applications ran on UNIX and AIX. Java Swing was used for graphical user interface, \nand Java  Remote Method Invocation (RMI) was used for communication between client \nand server.\n\n* Washington Information Network (WIN)\n      -  Developed Fish License application for the State of Washington (in C). The application ran on kiosks.\n      - Developed Your Hearing, Pay for College, Name Change applications for the State of Washington (in Java). \n\n* AIX Feature Group:\n      - Developed test plans, test procedures, test cases and test reports for Customer Environment Test (CET) and Installation Verification Test (IVT) of I/O, communication and mainframe-connectivity features for AIX on the RISC System 6000.\n\n* Simulation Interface Buffer (SIB) – Space Station Freedom\n       - Designed and developed applications used for simulation testing. The applications provided an interface between a host computer and device drivers running on IBM GearBox 800. The applications were developed in Ada and ran on Lynx OS.\n\n\n\n",
